      5 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تنصّر</span></b>  <i>He laboured,</i> or <i>strove, to aid,</i> or
<i>assist;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَالَجَ النَّصْرَ</span>: (M, K:) not of the
same category as <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَحَلَّمَ</span> [he endeavoured to acquire <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حِلْم</span>] and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تبرّر</span> [he endeavoured to characterize himself by <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِرّ</span>]. (M.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <i>He became a
Christian.</i> (M, K.)

